# Dynamic Web — Pokédex

A single-page Pokédex built with vanilla JavaScript and Vite, consuming the public [PokéAPI](https://pokeapi.co/). Browse, search, filter and sort Pokémon in either a card or table view, mark favorites, switch between light and dark themes, and build custom teams of six — all persisted to `localStorage` so your data is still there next time you open the app.

This repository is the deliverable for the *Dynamic Web* assignment (Erasmushogeschool Brussel — Applied Computer Science).

## Features

- **Two views** — toggle between a visual card grid and a sortable table (6+ columns).
- **Search** — instant filtering by Pokémon name.
- **Type filter** — narrow the list down to a single type, populated dynamically from the API.
- **Sort** — by ID, name, height, weight or base XP (ascending or descending).
- **Detail modal** — click any Pokémon for full stats, abilities, types and sprites.
- **Favorites** — mark any Pokémon to keep it in your personal collection (persisted to `localStorage`).
- **Team builder** — assemble named teams of six Pokémon from your favorites, with notes and form validation. Saved teams persist between sessions.
- **Theme toggle** — light/dark mode, remembered between visits.
- **Responsive design** — works on desktop, tablet and mobile.

## Tech stack

- **Vite** for the dev server and build pipeline
- **Vanilla JavaScript** (ES modules) — no framework
- **Plain CSS** with CSS variables for theming
- **[PokéAPI](https://pokeapi.co/)** as the data source
- **`localStorage`** for favorites, theme preference and saved teams

## Project structure

```
dynamic-web-pokedex/
├── public/              Static assets
├── src/                 Application source
│   └── main.js          Entry point
├── index.html           App shell, controls and modals
└── package.json
```

## Getting started

### Prerequisites

- [Node.js](https://nodejs.org/) 18 or newer
- npm (bundled with Node)

### Installation

```bash
git clone https://github.com/big-dawg-bit/dynamic-web-pokedex.git
cd dynamic-web-pokedex
npm install
```

### Run the dev server

```bash
npm run dev
```

The app will be available at the URL printed in the terminal (typically `http://localhost:5173`).

### Build for production

```bash
npm run build
```

The optimised output is written to `dist/`.

### Preview the production build

```bash
npm run preview
```

## How to use

1. Wait for the initial fetch to complete — the result counter updates from *Loading…* to the total number of Pokémon loaded.
2. Use the **search box** to filter by name, the **type dropdown** to filter by type, and the **sort dropdown** to reorder the list.
3. Switch between **Cards** and **Table** to change the layout.
4. Click any Pokémon to open the **detail modal**.
5. Click the favorite button on any Pokémon to add it to your favorites. Use the **Favorites** button at the top to show only those.
6. Click **Build Team** to open the team builder, pick six favorites, name your team and save it.
7. Click the theme button in the header to switch between light and dark mode.

